* The full version performed by {{wp|After the Rain (duo)|After the Rain}} was first released as a [[List of Pokémon digital singles#One, Two, Three (After the Rain)|digital single]] on December 15, 2019. It was produced by Mafumafu.
* The full version performed by Nishikawa-kun and Kirishō was first released as a [[List of Pokémon digital singles#One, Two, Three (Nishikawa-kun and Kirishō)|digital single]] on September 30, 2020. It was produced by Mafumafu.
* The full version performed by the Karaage Sisters was first released as a [[List of Pokémon digital singles#One, Two, Three (Karaage Sisters)|digital single]] on February 19, 2021.
* The full version performed in-character by [[Rica Matsumoto]] and [[Daiki Yamashita]] as {{Ash}} and [[Goh]] was first released as a [[List of Pokémon digital singles#One, Two, Three (Satoshi & Go)|digital single]] on March 16, 2022.

On the [[Pokémon TV Anime Theme Song BEST OF BEST OF BEST 1997-2023]] CD, 佐野弘明 ''{{jwp|佐野弘明|Hiroaki Sano}}'' and 毛谷村伸也 ''Shinya Keyamura'' were credited as additional producers.

==Opening animation: Version 1 ([[JN001]] – [[JN031]])==
===Synopsis===
The series logo appears as the camera pans across a large grassy hill and settles on {{Ash}}, [[Goh]], {{AP|Pikachu}}, and {{TP|Goh|Scorbunny}}, who are looking up at the sky. Ash and Pikachu are shown first, with Pikachu climbing around on his shoulders, jumping onto his shirt, and using it as a trampoline. Goh is then seen packing his [[bag]] with Scorbunny jumping at his side. [[Chloe]] is shown next poking her {{TP|Professor Cerise|Yamper}}, who then turns his head and causes Chloe to smile. A cut to [[Professor Cerise]] follows, who holds out three {{i|Poké Ball}}s. Ash, Goh, Pikachu, and Scorbunny are shown in front of maps featuring the [[first partner Pokémon]] of each of the [[region]]s from [[Kanto]] to [[Galar]] are shown.

Goh's hands are shown reaching towards a floating yellow orb, which is revealed to be {{p|Mew}}. Goh and Ash are then seen with their eyes meeting before each of them throw a Poké Ball in the air to send out a Pokémon. Ash, Pikachu, Chloe, Goh, and Scorbunny are seen dancing in the [[Cerise Laboratory]], while Yamper lies on the ground in front of Chloe. They then all clap and face the screen. Scorbunny, Pikachu, Ash, and Goh are then seen jumping off a brick terrace away from the lab and running down the street. They trip in front of Chloe, who turns and walks away. Ash and Goh, along with Pikachu and Scorbunny, are then seen gazing up at a rock from which {{MTR}}, [[Jessie]], [[James]], and {{TP|Jessie|Wobbuffet}} look down and sneer.

Pikachu jumps over a {{p|Tyranitar}} and uses {{m|Thunderbolt}} on it. Scorbunny then runs up to a {{p|Corviknight}} and uses {{m|Double Kick}} on it. Ash, Pikachu, [[Ren]], [[Chrysa]], Chloe, Professor Cerise, Goh, and Scorbunny all dance and clap their hands, Mew's shadow can be seen in the stained glass. A close-up of Pikachu and Scorbunny is shown, who smile and cry in quick succession. They are shown to be on top of Yamper, who is on top of [[Mimey]]. Pikachu and Scorbunny fall off of Yamper and Mimey catches them in each of his outstretched hands before all three jump off.

Ash, Goh, and Chloe, along with their partner {{OBP|Pokémon|species}}, are then seen walking on a rotating Poké Ball past several various Pokémon and landmarks from various regions. The following scene depends on the episode. Pikachu and Ash then jump into view, followed by Goh, Scorbunny, Pikachu, and Ash having tripped, with Goh skinning his knee. Goh and Scorbunny then jump into view, followed by all four seen standing up, looking at each other, and striking a pose.

