===Synopsis===
The intro starts with a {{p|Pidgey}} flying past [[Chloe]], [[Professor Cerise]], [[Chrysa]], [[Ren]], and finally {{Ash}} and [[Goh]]. Flashbacks of just before the two protagonists started their journeys are shown with Ash getting electrocuted by {{AP|Pikachu}} at [[Professor Oak's Laboratory]] and Goh seeing {{an|Mew}} for the first time. Cut to the present and Ash and Goh are leaving the [[Cerise Laboratory]] as they wave goodbye to Chloe. There are shots of the two going on journeys before Ash and Goh are seen in each of the eight core [[region]]s, each time including most, or all of the Pokémon Goh has [[List of Goh's Pokémon|caught]] that come from each of the regions.

A {{i|Poké Ball}} {{pkmn2|caught|catches}} something and one of the stars that hangs over the ball rises and turns into the same Mew that Goh is after, which he tries to reach out to grab. There is a zoom in on one of Goh's eyes and it transitions to Ash excitedly sending out his [[party]] in a stadium while wearing his [[Key Stone|Mega Glove]], [[Z-Power Ring]], and [[Dynamax Band]]. His Pokémon then battle an unknown opponent. Then Goh is seen with [[Danika]] and [[Quillon]] facing the six [[legendary giants]] on a [[Field Research|Trial Mission]] at the [[Split-Decision Ruins]] in the [[Crown Tundra]] for [[Project Mew]], before cutting back to Ash who is revealed to be battling {{an|Leon}}. Chloe is shown next doing a performance with her {{TP|Chloe|Eevee}} which ends with a fantasy of all of the [[Eeveelution]]s circling them.

{{TRT}} are then shown trying to capture Pikachu, before {{TP|Jessie|Wobbuffet}}, {{TP|James|Morpeko}}, and {{OBP|Pelipper|Team Rocket}} accidentally mess up their plans by appearing. Shots of past and present {{AP|friends}} and [[rival]]s of Ash's, as well as [[Wallace]], [[Lisia]], [[Horace]], and a familiar {{AP|Greninja}} are shown before going back to Ash's battle against Leon. Ash and Goh then interact with their Partner Pokémon before they run off with Ash's whole party and Goh's main Pokémon running alongside them as the opening ends.

