==Trivia==
* This was used as the opening theme for the most amount of consecutive episodes at 136 (surpassing [[Together]]'s previous record of 94 episodes).
** However, if one were to count the four versions of the song as different themes, this record would go to [[Best Wishes! (song)|Best Wishes!]] instead (84 episodes).
* One, Two, Three is the first opening to have more than two versions in a single series, as well as the first opening with multiple versions in a series to have different singers in different versions.
* The first version is the only opening of ''[[Pokémon Journeys: The Series]]'' to not feature any characters from a previous [[series]] other than {{Ash}}.
* The beginning of the song plays a sound that is similar to the [[Game Boy]] startup sound, possibly a reference to the earliest [[Pokémon games]] being on said console.
* A mashup of all four versions of the song was played at the 2023 [[Pocket Monsters Music Festival]].
* The lyrics {{tt|たとえ火の中　水の中|Tatoe hi no naka mizu no naka}} ''(Even if in fire, in water)'' were taken directly from the first Japanese opening theme, [[Aim to Be a Pokémon Master]]. 
* The first version of the song is available as DLC for the Rhythm Game "Taiko no Tatsujin Drum 'n' Fun".
* {{wp|Takanori Nishikawa}} posted on his Twitter account an [https://web.archive.org/web/20200809091110/https://twitter.com/TMR15/status/1292387867885309952 early version] of the second version of the opening animation, which has since been deleted. In it:
** The angle of the floor in the shot after the logo differs.
** {{AP|Pikachu}}'s tail is missing and Ash's [[bag|backpack]] and [[Chloe]]'s hair are redrawn in the distant shot of Ash, [[Goh]], and Chloe.
** Ash and Goh run further past the [[Cerise Laboratory]].
** The images of the [[legendary birds]] are rearranged.
** Glow, blur, fire, and sunray effects for the images of the [[Legendary Pokémon]] are not present.
** The snacks and papers are differently colored.
** The [[Poké Ball]]s in Goh's eye are not translucent.
** Goh's eye is not shaded.
** A yellow tint and sparkle effects are absent from the scene where Goh is surrounded by Poké Balls.
** The electricity effects from Goh's Poké Ball, {{p|Zapdos}}'s {{t|Electric}} attack, and Pikachu's {{m|Thunderbolt}} are purple.
** The legendary birds do not glow.
** The spotlights are yellow and the background is not darkened during Ash and Goh's battle.
** {{AP|Gengar}}'s {{m|Shadow Ball}} attack is not present.
** {{TP|Goh|Sobble}} fades out without a glow effect.
** The fire effect on {{TP|Goh|Raboot}}'s {{m|Ember|kick}} is not present.
** The sparkle effects in the background of Ash and Goh's parties are not present.
** {{p|Eternatus}} does not glow and the clouds do not glow purple.
** [[Raihan]]'s [[Rotom Phone]] is the standard color.
** The fire effect for [[Leon's Charizard]] and the darkening of the stadium is not present.
** The glow of {{p|Duraludon}}'s {{m|Steel Beam}} is not present.
** The icons and layout of the pictures from the Rotom Phone differ.
** A sparkle effect is added to {{p|Celebi}}.
** Fewer stars are visible in the forest at night.
** Darker shading on the shot of [[Vermilion City]] in the morning, lighter shading on the daytime, evening and nighttime shots of Vermilion.
** More stars are visible in Vermilion City at night.
** The sunray and water effects are missing from the ruins scene.
** Darker shading on the final shots of Ash, Goh, Pikachu, Raboot and both Trainers and their Pokémon.
* The third version of the opening animation marks {{Gary}}'s first appearance in an opening animation since [[High Touch!]].
* The first version of the opening is the only ''[[Pokémon Journeys: The Series]]'' opening to not feature {{an|Lana}}, {{an|Kiawe}}, {{an|Sophocles}} and {{an|Mallow}} in any form.
* [[Ash's Dracovish]] is his sole Pokémon on hand not to physically appear on the third version of the opening animation, as it only appears briefly in the final group sequence of characters.
* A remixed version of this song is used as {{mas|Ash}}'s battle theme during the {{DL|Special event|Challenge from Ash}} [[special event]] in {{g|Masters EX}}. Starting from the version 2.25.0 update, however, this music track has been removed from the game.
* Following [https://www3.nhk.or.jp/news/html/20221025/k10013869071000.html his arrest due to charges of attempted sexual assault] on October 24, 2022, Hidekazu Tanaka's arranger credit was omitted from the song credits beginning in [[JN130]]. Similarly, the opening and ending credits were removed from the [https://www.tv-tokyo.co.jp/anime/pocketmonster/staff/ staff listing on the TV Tokyo website] on October 25 and his name was removed from the [https://www.pokemon.co.jp/tv_movie/anime/ official Japanese Pokémon website] on October 28.
** His arranger credit was omitted from the [[Pokémon TV Anime Theme Song BEST OF BEST OF BEST 1997-2023]] CD, which was released after his arrest.

===Errors===
* During the {{pkmn|battle}} scene of the first version, {{TP|Goh|Scorbunny}}'s tail disappears for two frames.
* In the song credits for the second version, Hidekazu Tanaka is omitted. This is fixed beginning in [[JN034]].
* In the fourth version, Goh's {{p|Hoothoot}} and {{p|Kingdra}} are missing from the group shots of his Pokémon, while {{TP|Goh|Heracross}} is incorrectly included among the Pokémon that are based in [[Kanto]].
** Goh's {{p|Durant}} was initially omitted from the shot of his Pokémon that are based in [[Unova]]. However, this was corrected in [[JN102]].

